# Walkthrough - Fix TypeScript Error in CoreAdvisory

I have resolved the TypeScript assignment error in [CoreAdvisory.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/CoreAdvisory.tsx) by refactoring how icons are stored and rendered.

## Changes

### [components/services/CoreAdvisory.tsx](file:///Users/santiagovalencia/Documents/landing-siprac/landing-siprac/siprac-website/components/services/CoreAdvisory.tsx)

Refactored `advisoryServices` to store component references instead of JSX elements, and updated the render loop to instantiate them directly. This avoids the `React.cloneElement` type mismatch issue.

```diff
 const advisoryServices = [
     {
-        icon: <LayoutGrid className="size-8" />,
+        icon: LayoutGrid,
         title: 'Sistemas de Gestión Integrado (SGI)',
// ...
-                                       {React.cloneElement(service.icon as React.ReactElement, { className: "size-6 md:size-8" })}
+                                       <service.icon className="size-6 md:size-8" />
```

## Verification Results

### Automated Tests
- Validated that `lucide-react` icons function correctly as React components and accept `className` props.
- The syntax is valid JSX/TSX.
